1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,293
Accounting now runs on AI, automation, and blockchain.

2
00:00:04,343 --> 00:00:08,820
The accountant is no longer just a record keeper, but an analyst and advisor.

3
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:12,757
So, does learning with technology build more than technical skills?

4
00:00:14,157 --> 00:00:18,086
Employers see a gap between the skills they need and what graduates bring.

5
00:00:18,136 --> 00:00:22,771
Many programs still lean on theory, with limited hands-on use of digital tools.

6
00:00:22,821 --> 00:00:27,403
But past studies haven't shown how this technology actually builds competencies.

7
00:00:27,703 --> 00:00:31,032
Kolb's Experiential Learning says we learn best by doing.

8
00:00:31,082 --> 00:00:35,153
Siemens' Connectivism says knowledge grows through digital networks.

9
00:00:35,203 --> 00:00:39,500
And Bandura's Social Cognitive Theory says we learn by observing others.

10
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:42,994
Input: the respondents, and the competencies they need.

11
00:00:43,044 --> 00:00:46,511
Process: how technology-integrated education shaped them.

12
00:00:46,561 --> 00:00:50,222
Output: evidence-based strategies and policy recommendations.

13
00:00:50,522 --> 00:00:54,953
We focus on five competencies from the International Education Standards:

14
00:00:55,003 --> 00:00:59,553
intellectual, technical, personal, interpersonal, and organizational skills.

15
00:01:00,353 --> 00:01:07,427
Our null hypothesis: technology-integrated education has no significant relationship with these competencies.

16
00:01:07,727 --> 00:01:13,844
We use a mixed-methods, nested design: a survey measures the relationship, and interviews explain why.

17
00:01:14,744 --> 00:01:21,393
From 112 newly passed CPAs from PLV, Slovin's formula sets at least 88 respondents.

18
00:01:21,443 --> 00:01:27,425
All passed the board exam from 2023 to 2025, and work in accounting.

19
00:01:27,725 --> 00:01:32,730
They rate each statement on a four-point Likert scale, and ten join in-depth interviews.

20
00:01:33,030 --> 00:01:40,163
Weighted means describe their answers, correlation tests the relationship, and thematic analysis finds common themes.

21
00:01:40,863 --> 00:01:46,031
Participation is voluntary, and all data is protected under the Data Privacy Act.

22
00:01:46,331 --> 00:01:53,994
This study will help CPAs, students, educators, and PLV build an accounting education that keeps pace with technology.

23
00:01:54,294 --> 00:01:58,024
Because the accountant of the future needs more than technical skills.

